# Day 35/60 — AI Prompt Puzzle Challenge

## Objective

Today I built an AI Prompt Puzzle Challenge, an interactive application that teaches prompt engineering through practical exercises and progressively challenging scenarios.

Instead of reading theory, users improve their prompting skills by solving puzzles, reviewing performance reports, and experimenting with different prompt styles.

---

## What Was Generated

- AI Prompt Puzzle Challenge
- Interactive Prompt Engineering Exercises
- Multiple Difficulty Levels
- Prompt Performance Report
- Progress Dashboard
- Replayable Learning Experience
- Responsive HTML Application

---

## What I Learned

### Prompt Quality Matters

The effectiveness of AI responses depends heavily on how clearly a prompt communicates the task, context, and expected outcome.

### Learning by Doing

Interactive challenges are a far more effective way to understand prompt engineering than simply reading documentation.

### Small Changes Create Better Results

Minor improvements in wording, constraints, and examples can significantly improve AI outputs.

### Practice Builds Better Prompts

Consistently experimenting with prompts develops stronger communication skills when working with AI systems.

